<rml>
<head>
	<title>Table 06</title>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="../style.rcss"/>
	<link rel="help" href="https://www.w3.org/TR/2011/REC-CSS2-20110607/tables.html" />
	<meta name="Description" content="Flexible column widths, given by width percentages of 100% or more on the cells of the first table row." />
	<style>
		table {
			width: 300dp;
			margin-bottom: 12dp;
			color: #333;
			text-align: center;
		}
		td {
			border: 1dp #333;
			background: #cdd;
		}
		col { border: 1dp #333; }
	</style>
</head>

<body>
<p>100% / 200% on first-row cells.</p>
<table>
	<tr>
		<td style="width: 100%;">A</td>
		<td style="width: 200%;">B</td>
	</tr>
</table>

<p>100% / 200% / 300% on first-row cells.</p>
<table>
	<tr>
		<td style="width: 100%;">A</td>
		<td style="width: 200%;">B</td>
		<td style="width: 300%;">C</td>
	</tr>
</table>

<p>A fixed width on the col element takes precedence over a flexible width on the first-row cell.</p>
<table>
	<col style="width: 100dp;"/>
	<col/>
	<tr>
		<td style="width: 200%;">A</td>
		<td>B</td>
	</tr>
</table>

<p>A flexible width on a spanning first-row cell is distributed equally over the columns it spans.</p>
<table>
	<tr>
		<td style="width: 400%;" colspan="2">A</td>
		<td style="width: 100%;">B</td>
	</tr>
</table>
<handle size_target="#document"/>
</body>
</rml>
